        <obo:IAO_0000115 xml:lang="en">The cuticular invagination that is hollow.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000232 xml:lang="en">The apophysis in HAO refers to an ivagination of the cuticle that is cylindrical as opposed to a ridge that is elongate. Beutel et al. 2014 differentiate apodemes from apophyses in that apodemes are solid and apophyses are hollow.</obo:IAO_0000232>
        <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">cuticular apophysis</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
